"kind":"trace",
"id":"mask_walk",
"source":"mask_walk.py",
"code":"import sys\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    pos = 2\n    bit = [0] * n\n    for i in range(k):\n        room = int(data[pos])\n        bit[room] = 1 << i\n        pos += 1\n\n    mask = 0\n    for x in data[pos:]:\n        room = int(x)\n        mask = mask | bit[room]\n        print(room, mask)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
"alt":"The program reads a room count, the checkpoint rooms, then a route through the rooms. It gives each checkpoint room one bit, and for every room on the route it switches on that room's bit in mask, printing the room and the mask. Visiting a checkpoint changes the mask; visiting any other room leaves it alone, so the same room can appear with two different masks.",
"presets":[
